{
  "id": "GtaHospitalBillC01",
  "slug": "gta-hospital-bill/c01",
  "chapter": "Cold open",
  "topic": "What if you got the GTA6 hospital bill in real life?",
  "script": [
    {
      "beat": "garage roof",
      "text": "You jump off the garage roof. You land wrong. Everything goes grey. Then you blink, and you're standing outside the hospital doors. Not a scratch on you. Your phone buzzes. It's a bill. Ambulance: twelve hundred dollars. Emergency room: twenty-nine hundred. X-ray, cast, crutches. Total: six thousand, four hundred and eleven dollars."
    },
    {
      "beat": "skateboard",
      "text": "Mo's skateboard. The steepest hill in town. Grey. Hospital doors. Buzz. Eleven thousand."
    },
    {
      "beat": "bike and river",
      "text": "Your bike, a ramp made of planks, and the river. You don't make it. Grey. Doors. Buzz. Thirty-four thousand."
    },
    {
      "beat": "trampoline",
      "text": "Mo's trampoline, and the neighbour's greenhouse. Grey. Doors. Buzz. Nine thousand. The greenhouse is extra."
    },
    {
      "beat": "premise question",
      "text": "In the games, you crash, you wake up outside the hospital, they take a few hundred bucks, and you walk out whistling. So what would actually happen if you got the real hospital bill for living like a video game?"
    }
  ],
